---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import prompt from '../../docs/RESEARCH_SESSION_PROTOCOL_PROMPT.md?raw';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const internal = (segment) => `${base}/${segment.replace(/^\//, '')}`;
---
<Layout title="Memory Palace Protocol" description="The Agalmic Research Memory Palace Protocol v0.3 for standards-first provenance, intellectual-lineage review, epistemic authority, search-space mapping and decision replay.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Research operating protocol · v0.3</p>
      <h1>A memory palace for the research process, built on existing standards.</h1>
      <p class="lede">A platform-agnostic session prompt for preserving how research emerged while using W3C PROV, RO-Crate and CRediT wherever they already solve the problem. The local extension focuses narrowly on epistemic authority, lineage, handoff, search boundaries and roads not taken.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href={internal('downloads/Agalmic_Research_Memory_Palace_Protocol_v0.3.md')} download>Download v0.3 Markdown</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/TsatsuAmable/agalmicresearch/blob/main/docs/RESEARCH_SESSION_PROTOCOL_PROMPT.md">View canonical source ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">v0.3 correction</p>
        <h2>Provenance was already a field before we drew our graph.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">The protocol now explicitly treats the Memory Palace as an application profile and experimental extension.</p>
        <p>Use <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-dm/">W3C PROV</a> for ordinary provenance, <a href="https://credit.niso.org/">CRediT</a> for standardized scholarly contribution roles and <a href="https://www.researchobject.org/ro-crate/specification/1.3/">RO-Crate</a> for packaging research objects. Local fields are justified only where those systems do not adequately express the research question.</p>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/TsatsuAmable/agalmicresearch/blob/main/docs/STANDARDS_PROVENANCE_PROFILE.md">Read the standards-first profile ↗</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Novelty discipline</p>
        <h2>The protocol now searches the ancestors of an idea before celebrating its birth.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Novelty is a conclusion of search, not a tone of voice.</strong></p></div>
        <p>Every potentially publishable contribution must be classified against prior knowledge: established antecedent, independent rediscovery, synthesis, extension, application, operationalization, terminology candidate, novelty unassessed or candidate novelty. Exact-phrase novelty is not enough.</p>
        <p><a href={internal('lineage')}>Inspect the living lineage register →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Discovery attribution</p>
        <h2>Record the acts before deciding who discovered.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The protocol distinguishes <strong>candidate generation, significance recognition, validation, integration with prior knowledge and realization</strong>. Those events can belong to different humans, models, experts or institutions.</p>
        <p>W3C PROV can record the process without deciding the philosophical question of whether a current AI system is itself a knower or discoverer.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>Novelty belongs to the result relative to prior knowledge, not to the surprise of the actor who encountered it.</strong></p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Short activation</p>
        <h2>Use this when the full protocol is already available to the researcher or agent.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <blockquote class="activation">Activate the Agalmic Research Memory Palace Protocol v0.3. Treat this session as a versioned graph of discovery. Use W3C PROV, RO-Crate and CRediT where applicable, extending them only for genuinely missing epistemic fields. Track contribution provenance separately from epistemic authority; search intellectual lineage before claiming novelty; distinguish machine candidate generation from human or machine recognition, validation, integration and realization; preserve explored, rejected, deferred, surfaced-but-unexamined and scope-excluded branches; record reversal conditions, search boundaries, handoffs and publication/IP boundaries; and at closeout produce the complete Research Memory Palace Packet plus standards-compatible provenance outputs. Do not infer expertise, novelty or attribution without evidence, do not treat absent alternatives as rejected, and do not request or fabricate hidden chain-of-thought.</blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Canonical prompt</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>The complete operating protocol.</h2>
          <p>This page renders the repository source directly so the web view and canonical prompt cannot silently drift apart.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <pre class="protocol-text">{prompt}</pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Related infrastructure</p>
        <h2>The prompt feeds interoperable research objects.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Each provenance-complete session should now aim to emit a human-readable Memory Palace Packet, W3C PROV-compatible JSON-LD, CRediT role mappings, RO-Crate-compatible metadata and only then a small Agalmic extension patch for epistemic fields the standards cannot express.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href={internal('provenance')}>Explore provenance</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href={internal('lineage')}>Inspect lineage</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .protocol-text {
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
      border: 1px solid var(--rule, #c9c4b8);
      padding: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 2rem);
      font: 0.9rem/1.55 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.28);
      max-width: 100%;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }
    .activation {
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 1rem;
      border-left: 3px solid currentColor;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>